---
description: Mandatory onboarding before any code change in LifePlate
alwaysApply: true
---

Before editing code or exploring the codebase:

1. Read `/AGENTS.md` at the repo root
2. Read `docs/architecture.md` for system overview
3. Read the package `AGENTS.md` for every area you will touch:
   - `apps/mobile/AGENTS.md`
   - `apps/api/AGENTS.md`
   - `packages/shared/AGENTS.md`
4. Read `docs/database.md` if changing schema or migrations
5. Read `docs/conventions.md` for patterns and tests

Do not blindly traverse the codebase when these docs answer the question.

When you change architecture, routes, or conventions, update the relevant doc in the same PR.
